<header class="start-masthead"><p class="eyebrow">Lab runtime · proposed documentation</p><h1>Runtime architecture and ownership</h1><p>Follow the executable paths and the independent stores they own.</p><p class="source-note">Draft prepared on 2026-10-14. Integration and final T21 qualification remain pending.</p></header>

<section id="runtime-architecture-two-entrypaths" aria-labelledby="runtime-architecture-two-entrypaths-title"><h2 id="runtime-architecture-two-entrypaths-title">Two entrypaths</h2>

<p>The admitted local CLI enters lab.py, then cli.main. With no selected store, read_data captures the frozen repository envelope; explicit init constructs a local store. Review/sign/apply/replay/recover and ephemeral Session are local store operations.</p>

<p>The captured Base stdio API enters serve.main and constructs a Base service after independent source/profile/policy/nonce checks. IntegrationService composes Base28, Action3 and Governance3 with the same Schemas object and independent authenticated branch contexts. A Base connection cannot advertise full34 readiness. The <a href="research/sources/product/lab/release-candidates/v1/interface/composite-operator-v1-completion-0001/revision-0003/README.md">maintained composite candidate</a> supplies a separately selected serialized launcher contract.</p>

<figure id="components"><pre><code class="language-mermaid">flowchart LR
  CLI[Admitted local CLI] --&gt; LS[Local transaction store / HEAD]
  CALL[Exact stdio envelope] --&gt; F[Composite IntegrationService]
  F --&gt; B[Base Service 28]
  F --&gt; A[Action Service 3]
  F --&gt; G[Governance Service 3]
  B --&gt; W[Owned workspace journal]
  B --&gt; R[Signed readers / native replay]
  R --&gt; C[Context / ephemeral Session]
  A --&gt; AJ[Action grant / effect journal]
  G --&gt; GS[Selected native governance store]
  R -. derive .-&gt; Q[SQLite / graph views]</code></pre><figcaption>The CLI owns a separate local transaction store. The composite routes unchanged calls to three independently authenticated branches. Base workspace, Action effects and native Governance state are distinct; readers derive Context and disposable query representations.</figcaption><p>Explanatory component/sequence map, not a declaration of new ontology relation kinds or qualified runtime execution.</p></figure>

</section>

<section id="runtime-architecture-ten-implementation-areas" aria-labelledby="runtime-architecture-ten-implementation-areas-title"><h2 id="runtime-architecture-ten-implementation-areas-title">Ten implementation areas</h2>

<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Concrete responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>lab-runtime</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-runtime/v1/lab_runtime/cli.py">CLI</a>, source selection, local transaction/replay/recovery, graph, Session</td></tr><tr><td>lab-provisioning</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-provisioning/candidates/v1/provision.py">Pinned scoped branch</a> and configuration/HEAD selection</td></tr><tr><td>lab-bootstrap</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-bootstrap/candidates/v1/bootstrap.py">Seed/package composition</a> and controlled candidate changes</td></tr><tr><td>lab-integration</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-integration/candidates/v1/validate.py">Composition verification</a>, distinct from component admission</td></tr><tr><td>lab-review</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-review/candidates/v1/review.py">Bounded review material</a>, not an actual owner decision</td></tr><tr><td>lab-context</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-context/candidates/v1/native_reader.py">Native reader</a> and <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-context/candidates/v1/context.py">generator/consumer</a></td></tr><tr><td>lab-ontology</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-ontology/candidates/v1/adapters/native/src/lib.rs">Semantic/governance event replay</a> and represented views</td></tr><tr><td>lab-continuity</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-continuity/candidates/v2/custody.py">Durable custody evidence</a> without restoring live memory</td></tr><tr><td>lab-work</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-work/candidates/v1/episode.py">Bounded episode</a> and public evidence/archive verification</td></tr><tr><td>lab-workflows</td><td><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-workflows/candidates/v1/workflows/engineering.py">Engineering</a>, <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-workflows/candidates/v1/workflows/research.py">research</a>, <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-workflows/candidates/v1/authority/evaluator.py">authority</a>, <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-workflows/candidates/v1/authority/dispatch.py">dispatch</a> and learning</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p>These are implementation responsibilities. Candidate carriers, actual effects and effective admission retain their own records.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-architecture-the-call-chain" aria-labelledby="runtime-architecture-the-call-chain-title"><h2 id="runtime-architecture-the-call-chain-title">The call chain</h2>

<p>The Base service verifies channel, byte/envelope/profile bounds, allowed operation, call ID, actor, strictest deadline, budgets, cut, domain schema and actual selected code. An effectful request claims an exact fingerprint/key in the owned Vault. Prior outcomes return before fresh allocation; pending outcomes are not redispatched.</p>

<p>Source selection names the actual source, reader, mapper, Context producer, package, Principal and period. Native replay verifies original histories; a mapper produces a source-bound projection; Context is generated under current policy; a live Session/Machine borrows only what its actual resource permits. No internal adapter nickname can replace those public identities.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-architecture-state-ownership-and-dependencies" aria-labelledby="runtime-architecture-state-ownership-and-dependencies-title"><h2 id="runtime-architecture-state-ownership-and-dependencies-title">State ownership and dependencies</h2>

<p>Local immutable transactions/HEAD, native event histories, private API journal material, derived SQLite/graph files and ephemeral Session RAM have separate owners and recovery contracts. The <a href="runtime-state-memory.html">state/authority/memory page</a> follows those stores without drawing them as one database.</p>

<p>The selected interpreter/native/library closure is independent of code/source/profile selection. Full historical provenance and the narrower schema execution dependency table remain explicit; unavailable historical inputs are not silently aliased to current files. Fresh original guards remain required even when pure preparation reuses a scoped snapshot.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-architecture-current-integration-standing" aria-labelledby="runtime-architecture-current-integration-standing-title"><h2 id="runtime-architecture-current-integration-standing-title">Current integration standing</h2>

<p>The eight API17 overlay leaves are reviewed code, not current all34 qualification. The old execution capture is ineligible. Family4&#x27;s Source table bound future-changing API preparation files, so final publication would invalidate the family. The capture guard rejects that cycle.</p>

<p>A successor needs exact historical snapshot technical bindings and complete preserved native history/role/code proof. The driver4 private loader and margin component have scoped peer checks; no successful complete learning/empirical margin follows. See <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T07/api17-task-local-capture-0004/independent-review-0001.json">the capture flag</a> and <a href="runtime-status.html">dated status</a>.</p>

</section>

